  "interpretation": "Static MoGe depth at fixed lambda_depth=0.5 degraded the five-view pilot: holdout PSNR 17.73 to 15.18 dB; registered lidar MAE 2.82 to 7.83 m, RMSE 4.17 to 10.66 m. The rendered DSM is nearly flat, with roofs lost. Registration found a 38.94 m horizontal shift and retained only 84.1% coverage, so its offset is not a reliable placement estimate and the registered error uses a reduced overlap. Unregistered median error is +16.80 m. MoGe priors on near-orthographic satellite views are weak; their visible roof shapes did not translate into useful geometry with this masked Pearson loss. The loss includes zero-filled padding, so a small depth loss alone does not demonstrate correct surface shape. Keep the five-view baseline; no lambda tuning used the holdout or lidar. One block, one lidar of unknown date; no production or broader independent accuracy claim.",
